  "body": "This PR adds some steps to dispatch a close event of MessagePort API.\r\nAs discussed in #1766, there is currently no timely and reliable way to detect when a MessagePort becomes disentangled. This makes it difficult to release resources associated with ports.  \r\nSo,[ we proposed adding a close event](https://github.com/fergald/explainer-messageport-close#). For example, if there are two entangled ports, portA and portB, and portA is closed, the close event is fired on portB.\r\n\r\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\r\n   * Chrome\r\n   * https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/914\r\n   * https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/271\r\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\r\n   * Chromium: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/5003089\r\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\r\n   * Chromium: [1495616](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1495616)\r\n   * Gecko: [1874820](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1874820)\r\n   * WebKit: [267567](https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=267567)\r\n   * Deno: [21964](https://github.com/denoland/deno/issues/21964)\r\n   * Node.js: [51496](https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/51496)\r\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/517\r\n- [ ] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use. <!-- If you created this PR from a single commit, Github copied its message. Otherwise, you need to add a commit message yourself. -->\r\n\r\nPlease take a look @domenic  @asutherland @annevk\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\r\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\r\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\r\n\r\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\r\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\r\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\r\n    and remove what's below.\r\n-->\r\n***\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9933/document-lifecycle.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 12, 2024, 8:01 AM UTC (77a7c7f)\">/document-lifecycle.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9933/41c1f94...77a7c7f/document-lifecycle.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 12, 2024, 8:01 AM UTC (77a7c7f)\">diff</a> )\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9933/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 12, 2024, 8:01 AM UTC (77a7c7f)\">/index.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9933/41c1f94...77a7c7f/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 12, 2024, 8:01 AM UTC (77a7c7f)\">diff</a> )\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9933/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 12, 2024, 8:01 AM UTC (77a7c7f)\">/indices.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9933/41c1f94...77a7c7f/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 12, 2024, 8:01 AM UTC (77a7c7f)\">diff</a> )\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9933/web-messaging.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 12, 2024, 8:01 AM UTC (77a7c7f)\">/web-messaging.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9933/41c1f94...77a7c7f/web-messaging.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jan 12, 2024, 8:01 AM UTC (77a7c7f)\">diff</a> )",
